---
import ResidenceLayout from "../../../layouts/ResidenceLayout.astro";
import { frederick } from "../../../data/residences/frederick";
---

<ResidenceLayout
  residence={frederick}
  title="Resident handbook · Frederick Cottage | Mt Cottages"
  description="Frederick Cottage resident handbook: expectations, policies, payments, maintenance, and emergency guidance."
  eyebrow="Frederick Cottage · Handbook"
  heading="The handbook for living here."
  lede="Expectations, policies, and support paths — written for the resident, kept general where arrangements vary."
>
  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="site-width prose">
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Living here well</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>Frederick Cottage hosts 30+ day furnished stays. Treat it as a home on a residential street: tidy entry and lawn rhythm, considerate noise, and care for furnishings, kitchen, and laundry.</p>
          <ul><li>Kitchen: clean as you go; confirm consumables, dishwasher, and trash placement.</li><li>Laundry: confirm machine use, supplies, and lint/dryer care on arrival.</li><li>Outdoors: keep entry clear; confirm grill, furniture, and yard expectations.</li><li>Smoking, guests, and pets follow the written arrangement — ask before assuming.</li></ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Policies</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>An inquiry is a conversation, not a lease or approval. Any later screening, agreement, payment schedule, or approval is a separate step with its own documents.</p>
          <ul><li>Stay length: 30 days or longer as the baseline; short-term pricing by inquiry.</li><li>Payments: use the instructions tied to the agreement; never email card or bank details.</li><li>Privacy: do not submit Social Security numbers or sensitive documents via the public form.</li><li>Household: occupants, pets, and accessibility needs agreed in advance.</li></ul>
          <div class="cluster"><a class="button button--ghost" href="/privacy.html">Privacy</a><a class="text-link" href="/faq.html">Common questions</a></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Maintenance & emergencies</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>Non-emergency: submit a clear request with home, location, problem, timing, and helpful photos. Emergency (fire, active gas smell, major flooding, immediate danger): call 911 first, then resident support.</p>
          <div class="cluster"><a class="button button--ghost" href="/maintenance.html">Maintenance</a><a class="text-link" href="/emergency-maintenance.html">Emergency guidance</a></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="prose-section reveal">
        <h2>Payments & portal</h2>
        <div class="stack">
          <p>Current residents use the portal, rent, and support paths tied to their agreement. Links stay general here because methods vary by arrangement.</p>
          <div class="cluster"><a class="text-link" href="/resident-portal.html">Resident portal</a><a class="text-link" href="/pay-rent.html">Pay rent</a><a class="text-link" href="/residents.html">Resident resources</a></div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</ResidenceLayout>
